During the lunch break, I quickly go to the supermarket.
I take my backpack with me.
We are having a barbecue in the park tonight.
I buy potato chips and the bread rolls for the three of us.
Unfortunately, the supermarket is very full today.
I stand at the checkout for ages.
A man in front of me slowly counts his money: one euro, two euros...
Finally it is my turn and I pay.
"Do you need the till receipt?" the cashier asks.
I nod, and he gives me the till receipt.
On the way back to the office, I grumble in my head.
The queue at the checkout was really incredibly long!
I had absolutely no patience left at the end.
The man in front of me paid entirely with coins!
But I quickly forget the stress again.
It is really hot today, perfect for the summer.
I am already looking forward to the barbecue with Jonas and Nele.
